2011-05-20	fselman		mefpp-1.5
	- working on clone of version in Bitbucket
	repository. This version has major modifications
	to the WCS sectin. It should be given relatively
	good astrometry for WFI at PA=0 degrees.

2011-04-29	fselman		mefpp-1.4

	- Added split function. A set of MEF files
	can be split without any further processing.

	- Tested BPM function. The system create a BPM
	such that a bad pixel has value 0 and a good one
	has a value 1. It uses a BPM with the oposite
	identification.

	- Modified to read configuration from file.
	No need for wfi.h. Now in the directory
	where the data is being processed there
	should be a file named mefpp.paf. This file
	could be a symbolic link: meffpp.paf -> wfi.paf,
	or mefpp.paf -> omegacam.paf.

	- qfits/src/pafs.c was modified so that
	the routine query_paf closes the file
	that it opens.

	- mefpp modified so that bias and bpm creation
	can be run stand alone.

	- TODO: clean the logic so that the recipe can
	be called in the following configurations:

		- mefpp --split splitlist.txt
		(only split files)

		- mefpp --bias biaslist.txt --biassave
		(it assumes presence of BPMs)

		- mefpp --dome <> (with default values for other cal frames)

		- mefpp  --sky <> (with default values for other cal frames)

		- mefpp --mff <> (with default values for other cal frames)

		- mefpp --science <> (with default values for cal frames)

2011-03-29	fselman		mefpp-1.2
	- Added a "!" in front of the bmp command in the
	routine that creates the master flat field in
	mefp_lib.c. This fixes a bug that with the 
	BPM in use we were choosing the bad pixels.
	This issue should be addresses in a more general
	way by allowing the user to select how a
	"0" in the BPM will be interpreted.

2011-03-25	fselman		mefpp-1.1
	- Used eclipse 5.0.0 which is the latest version,
	together with qfits-5.4.0 which is the latest
	version compatible with eclipse (it uses the
	function xmemory).
	- Modified the sysconf.c routines to configure
	the system to use gcc for os_darwin, and to
	include the CFLAG "-m32" to force 32 bits in
	machines that can compile both.
	- Modified tutorial document.
	- Added directory ins/mef/static_cal together
	with a set of BPM fits file that can be used
	for testing.
